{"title":"Reims and Amiens","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/920529695/0/marginalrevolution~Reims-and-Amiens.html","date":1750480100000,"content":"<p>Both cities have significant war histories, but they are very different to visit, even though they are only two hours apart by car.</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reims\" target=\"_blank\">Reims</a> was largely destroyed in World War I, and so the central core was rebuilt in the 1920s, with <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=f7661461505a9ca6&amp;q=reims+art+deco&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=AIIjpHxU7SXXniUZfeShr2fp4giZ1Y6MJ25_tmWITc7uy4KIemkjk18Cn72Gp24fGkjjh6xBoibEaR8uzvPi9MPqTLIFFRz8Nrq6LqOK7ioaVKk7Pt4hQmHoQggRFoCqaJYQKIR-UPOO0v_oJBCfBk1TonINX1AWeVVt_FczIWpWaBeM2SWo1H4Ih69bNSWssixzZjhPuWKf&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjfk-XI24COAxUxTqQEHeFxCRkQtKgLegQIExAB&amp;biw=1280&amp;bih=585&amp;dpr=1.5\" target=\"_blank\">a partial Art Deco look</a>.  The downtown is attractive and prosperous, the people look sharp and happy, and it is a university town.  You arrive and feel the place is a wonderful success.  If you had to live in a mid-sized French city, you might choose this one.</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.google.com/search?q=reims+cathedral&amp;sca_esv=f7661461505a9ca6&amp;udm=2&amp;biw=1280&amp;bih=585&amp;ei=9rNVaOHeKaCskdUP6eKEoAo&amp;ved=0ahUKEwjhsZvK24COAxUgVqQEHWkxAaQQ4dUDCBE&amp;uact=5&amp;oq=reims+cathedral&amp;gs_lp=EgNpbWciD3JlaW1zIGNhdGhlZHJhbDIFEAAYgAQyBRAAGIAEMgUQABiABDIFEAAYgAQyBRAAGIAEMgUQABiABDIFEAAYgAQyBRAAGIAEMgUQABiABDIFEAAYgARInCVQ_QVY1B5wAXgAkAEBmAGQAaABpAuqAQQxMS42uAEDyAEA-AEBmAINoALWCMICBhAAGAcYHsICBhAAGAgYHsICCBAAGAgYChgewgIGEAAYBRgemAMAiAYBkgcDNy42oAegWrIHAzYuNrgHzQjCBwQyLTEzyAcz&amp;sclient=img\" target=\"_blank\">The main cathedral</a> is one of the best in France, and arguably in the world.  <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.google.com/search?q=reims+basilica+interior&amp;sca_esv=f7661461505a9ca6&amp;udm=2&amp;biw=1280&amp;bih=585&amp;ei=MbRVaPD-A87_nsEP8-bF4AE&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiw24bm24COAxXOvycCHXNzERwQ4dUDCBE&amp;uact=5&amp;oq=reims+basilica+interior&amp;gs_lp=EgNpbWciF3JlaW1zIGJhc2lsaWNhIGludGVyaW9ySMgsUOUFWKwncAF4AJABAZgBkAKgAecUqgEGMTUuOS4yuAEDyAEA-AEBmAIMoALpCsICChAAGIAEGEMYigXCAgYQABgHGB7CAgUQABiABMICBhAAGAoYHsICBBAAGB7CAgYQABgFGB7CAgYQABgIGB7CAggQABgIGAoYHpgDAIgGAZIHBTcuMi4zoAeTXbIHBTYuMi4zuAfgCsIHBjAuMS4xMcgHLg&amp;sclient=img\" target=\"_blank\">The lesser-known basilica</a> also is top tier.  There are scattered Roman ruins.  French kings were coronated in Reims from early on, all the way up through 1825.</p>\r\n<p>Amiens is on the Somme, and <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Amiens_(1918)\" target=\"_blank\">the 1916 Battle of the Somme</a>, followed by a later 1918 offensive, was a turning point in WWI history.  The town is a melange of architectural styles, with <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amiens-tourisme.com/en/incontournables/saint-leu-quarter/\" target=\"_blank\">many half-timbered homes</a> but also scattered works from different centuries.  The town also has <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tour_Perret_(Amiens)\" target=\"_blank\">France’s “first skyscraper,”</a> renowned in its time but now a rather short and out of place embarrassment.  The main <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=f7661461505a9ca6&amp;q=amiens+cathedral&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=AIIjpHxU7SXXniUZfeShr2fp4giZ1Y6MJ25_tmWITc7uy4KIeuYzzFkfneXafNx6OMdA4MQRJc_t_TQjwHYrzlkIauOKiWCnruNfHTRmzt0RxosbrOMpYTFDxPGyD8T2B3g2diIu3ngkbY9zBvCWUufXsTFwoiRfzCo6PN174qxy5RWVWKD-YXE&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjk6-qh2oCOAxVQUqQEHZhBGAQQtKgLegQIERAB&amp;biw=1280&amp;bih=585&amp;dpr=1.5\" target=\"_blank\">Amiens cathedral</a>, however, is perhaps the best in all of France.</p>\r\n<p>The town itself feels like visiting a banlieu, with large numbers of African and Muslim immigrants.  It is lively, and it feels as if a revitalization is underway, though I do understand opinions on these matters differ.  Real estate prices <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://chatgpt.com/share/6855b59b-ae18-8010-bf41-912b173df77e\" target=\"_blank\">are at about 3x their 1990s levels</a>.  That to me is strong evidence that things are going well.</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.google.com/search?q=Restaurant+Momos+Tibetian+amiens&amp;sca_esv=f7661461505a9ca6&amp;ei=3rVVaMibFoCHkdUP0Zy_4AM&amp;ved=0ahUKEwjIguGy3YCOAxWAQ6QEHVHODzwQ4dUDCBA&amp;uact=5&amp;oq=Restaurant+Momos+Tibetian+amiens&amp;gs_lp=Egxnd3Mtd2l6LXNlcnAiIFJlc3RhdXJhbnQgTW9tb3MgVGliZXRpYW4gYW1pZW5zMgoQABiwAxjWBBhHMgoQABiwAxjWBBhHMgoQABiwAxjWBBhHMgoQABiwAxjWBBhHMgoQABiwAxjWBBhHSKgQULkFWKEKcAF4AZABAJgBAKABAKoBALgBA8gBAPgBAZgCAaACBpgDAOIDBRIBMSBAiAYBkAYFkgcBMaAHALIHALgHAMIHAzItMcgHBA&amp;sclient=gws-wiz-serp\" target=\"_blank\">Restaurant Momos Tibetian</a> has excellent Chinese and Tibetan food.  The Picardy museum has some very good works by Boucher, Balthus, Picabia, El Greco, and Chavannes.</p>\r\n<p>Both cities are radically undervisisted.  They do attract some tourists, but for the most part you feel you have them to yourself.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/06/reims-and-amiens.html\">Reims and Amiens</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/920529695/0/marginalrevoluti